INSERT INTO artefact (artefact_id, project_id, version, file_path, content_type, content, size_bytes, created_by, created_at) VALUES ('6bbbd6c8-d04c-48ea-8d34-44ea632b9af2', '03735ad1-8759-414e-a93f-ce8cc7bfc1fc', 1, 'feedback/ITERATION_REPORT_P01_i1.md', 'text/markdown', '# Iteration Report — Pipeline 01 — Iteration 1
**Agent:** Pipeline 01 Requirements Agent
**Prompt Version:** v7/PIPELINE_01_REQUIREMENTS_DISCOVERY
**Iteration Number:** 1
**Date:** 2026-05-31
**Project:** QABOT-001 — Q & A Interop Bot
---
## Session Scores
| Dimension | Score (1–5) | Notes |
|-----------|-------------|-------|
| Output quality overall | N/A | User skipped feedback |
| Eval spec specificity (checks were concrete, not vague) | N/A | User skipped feedback |
| Guardrail accuracy (right IDs, right checks) | N/A | User skipped feedback |
| Coverage completeness (nothing important missed) | N/A | User skipped feedback |
| EMIS-X platform mandate accuracy | N/A | User skipped feedback |
| Regulatory citation quality (IDs/clauses, no bare assertions) | N/A | User skipped feedback |
**North Star Score:** N/A (feedback skipped)
---
## Requirements Produced
| REQ ID | Title | Checks Generated | Under-specified? |
|--------|-------|-----------------|-----------------|
| REQ-001 | Conversational Q&A Chat Widget | 8 | No |
| REQ-002 | Escalation to Human Support | 7 | No |
| REQ-003 | Full-Page Chat Mode | 5 | No |
| REQ-004 | Documentation Indexing via CI | 5 | No |
| REQ-005 | Conversation Management | 5 | No |
| REQ-006 | Bot Loading & Status States | 5 | No |
**Total requirements:** 6
**Total checks:** ~35 across all requirements
**Requirements with < 3 checks:** None
**Requirements with no concrete input/output values:** None
---
## Gaps Identified
1. **REQ-001 authentication gap:** The initial REQ-001 draft was saved without EMIS-X authentication requirement. This was only confirmed mid-session during REQ-003 discussion. Required a v2 save to correct. The prompt should probe for authentication requirements earlier — ideally during Phase 2 or at the start of Phase 5 before the first requirement is confirmed.
2. **Rate limiting captured as NFR only:** Rate limiting (50 messages/session, 200/day) was captured as a non-functional requirement rather than as a standalone requirement with an eval spec. Downstream coding agents will have no deterministic checks for rate limiting enforcement. Consider whether this warrants a REQ-007.
3. **Degraded mode (bot outage → escalation form) not captured as a requirement:** This behaviour was mentioned in Phase 6 NFRs but never formalised as a requirement with acceptance criteria and eval checks. It is a meaningful UX behaviour that Pipeline 05 will need to design.
4. **AWS SES silent failure behaviour** captured in integration points but not as an acceptance criterion in REQ-002. A coding agent implementing REQ-002 might not know to handle SES failure silently.
5. **Teams webhook retry policy** deferred to Pipeline 03 without a default assumption. If Pipeline 03 doesn''t address it, the behaviour on transient webhook failure is undefined.
---
## Prompt Improvement Recommendations
| # | Section | Current behaviour | Recommended change | Priority |
|---|---------|-------------------|-------------------|----------|
| 1 | Phase 5 — Dimension 3: Security | Authentication is probed per-requirement but not asked globally upfront | Add a global authentication question at the start of Phase 5: "Does this system require authentication to access any part of it? If yes, what mechanism?" — so auth is established as a baseline before individual requirements are confirmed | HIGH |
| 2 | Phase 5 — Requirements Elicitation | Integration failure modes (SES silent fail, webhook user-visible fail) are captured in Phase 7 but not fed back into the relevant requirement''s acceptance criteria | After Phase 7, add a sweep: "For each integration point with a defined failure mode, check whether that failure mode is captured as an acceptance criterion in the relevant REQ. If not, update the REQ." | HIGH |
| 3 | Phase 6 — NFR sweep | Rate limiting captured as NFR without eval spec | If rate limiting is confirmed, prompt: "Should this be a standalone requirement with deterministic checks (e.g. HTTP 429 on limit exceeded), or remain as an NFR?" | MEDIUM |
| 4 | Phase 10.5 — Cross-cutting gate | Degraded mode captured in NFRs but not as a requirement | Add "degraded mode / graceful degradation" as an explicit cross-cutting concern in the Phase 10.5 gate checklist | MEDIUM |
| 5 | Phase 5 — per-requirement confirmation | Auth correction required a v2 save | Do not save a requirement until all four dimensions (including security/auth) are fully confirmed — save only on explicit user "yes" after full dimension review | LOW |
---
## Regulatory Citation Gaps
- `manifest.md`, Constraints section: GDPR Article 6 lawful basis for escalation email processing correctly tagged as `[UNVERIFIED — IG-OWNER: TBD — RESOLUTION DATE: TBD — GO-LIVE BLOCKER]` ✅
- `REQ-002.md`, Dimension 2: GDPR Article 6 lawful basis correctly flagged as unverified ✅
- No bare regulatory assertions identified — all claims carry either a Guardrail ID or an UNVERIFIED tag ✅
---
## Expert Corrections
```
CORRECTION-1:
  Location: REQ-001 — Dimension 3: Security
  Agent produced: "No authentication required to use widget; HTTPS in transit"
  Expert corrected to: "EMIS-X authentication required for all access to widget and full-page view; unauthenticated access blocked with redirect to EMIS-X login"
  Reason: Authentication requirement was confirmed by the user during REQ-003 discussion and applied retroactively. The agent should have probed for authentication before confirming REQ-001.
  Pattern: ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA
```
---
## Downstream Agent Impact
1. **Pipeline 03 — AI implementation approach undefined:** This is the highest-risk blocker. Pipeline 03 cannot complete architecture without deciding LLM vs RAG vs embeddings. The 2-sprint timebox makes this urgent.
2. **Pipeline 03 — Rate limiting enforcement point:** Client-side, API gateway, or bot service — undefined. Pipeline 03 must decide and add architecture-level checks.
3. **Pipeline 04 — AWS SES failure handling:** The silent failure behaviour for SES is described in the integration points table but is not an acceptance criterion in REQ-002. Pipeline 04 should add this to the API contract for the escalation endpoint.
4. **Pipeline 05 — Degraded mode UX:** Bot outage → escalation form is a meaningful UX state not captured as a requirement. Pipeline 05 PxD will need to design this state without a formal requirement to reference.
5. **Pipeline 07 — GDPR lawful basis blocker:** REQ-002 carries an unverified IG-003 lawful basis. Pipeline 07 normalisation will flag this as a go-live blocker during JSON transformation.
---
## Human Review Checklist
- [ ] Regulatory citations verified against source documents
- [x] Expert corrections recorded above (1 correction — REQ-001 auth gap)
- [ ] HIGH priority prompt recommendations reviewed and approved
- [x] Iteration report saved via `save_artefact` with `feedback/` file path
- [ ] Agent team notified of prompt changes required (2 HIGH priority items identified)
', 7050, 'ern:emis:user:user:7ae7b859-c480-4644-b3be-d77d628f6e7e', '2026-05-31 19:47:50.916603+00');
INSERT INTO artefact (artefact_id, project_id, version, file_path, content_type, content, size_bytes, created_by, created_at) VALUES ('b73ada95-280e-47d2-9416-ce154f3f14f2', '03735ad1-8759-414e-a93f-ce8cc7bfc1fc', 3, 'manifest.md', 'text/markdown', '# Q & A Interop Bot — Requirements Manifest
**Version:** 1.0
**Created:** 2026-05-31
**Project Code:** QABOT-001
**Regulatory Classification:** Not safety-critical
**Compliance Domain:** Generic
---
## Product Overview
The Q & A Interop Bot is a conversational chat agent embedded in the existing partner portal (built on Astro/Starlight with a React wrapper). It indexes interoperability documentation and answers external partner developers'' questions by reformulating content in clearer language with concrete examples — rather than quoting documentation verbatim.
The bot is available as a floating widget in the bottom-right corner on every portal page and as a dedicated full-page experience at a fixed portal route. Both modes require EMIS-X authentication. When the bot cannot answer from the indexed documentation, it escalates the query to the internal team via a Teams webhook notification and sends a confirmation email to the partner developer via AWS SES.
**Core Problem Solved:**
Internal developers are spending approximately 20% of sprint time answering repetitive interop capability questions from external partners. This is causing developer burnout, backlog delays, and potential partner revenue loss. The bot targets reducing this to under 5% of sprint time.
**Primary Users:**
- **External partner developers:** Primary audience — technically literate developers (junior to senior) integrating with EMIS APIs and the SMART-on-FHIR-style app launch system
- **Internal staff:** Secondary beneficiaries — freed from answering repetitive questions
---
## Global Standards
### Design System
- **Primary Colour:** NHS Blue (#005EB8)
- **Border Radius:** 8px
- **Typography:** TBD — defined in Pipeline 05 PxD
- **Spacing:** 8px grid system
### Technical Standards
- **Authentication:** EMIS-X OAuth2
- **API Protocol:** REST over HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
- **Infrastructure:** AWS, eu-west-2 region
- **Email:** AWS SES
- **Notifications:** Microsoft Teams webhook
- **CI/CD:** GitHub Actions
- **Encryption:** TLS 1.2+ in transit; AES-256-GCM for any special category data at rest (N/A for this system)
### Genesis AI Skills (Applicable Guardrails)
**Information Governance:**
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — only necessary data collected and returned in all requirements
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — GDPR Article 6 lawful basis required for personal data processing
**Security:**
- **AUTH-004:** Authorisation Required — EMIS-X authentication enforced on all chat access points
- **SEC-001:** TLS Encryption — all HTTP communication over TLS 1.2+
- **WSEC-006a:** URL Encoding — encodeURIComponent() for all user-supplied URL values
- **WSEC-013:** Security Headers — @emisgroup/acp-security-headers in package.json
**Observability:**
- OTEL instrumentation required for all critical paths (chat query, escalation, indexing)
- Span naming convention: `qabot.{feature}.{action}.{state}`
### EMIS-X Platform Standards (Frontend — Non-Negotiable)
| Mandate | Guardrail | Version/Note |
|---|---|---|
| **Package manager:** pnpm only — pnpm-lock.yaml required | WA-005 | No npm/yarn |
| **Components:** `@emisgroup/ui-*` — no native button/input/select/textarea/table/dialog/fieldset/legend/form | DS-001 | Import from @emisgroup/ui-* |
| **Colours:** `var(--token-*)` only in CSS/SCSS — no hardcoded hex/rgb/hsl | DS-002 | Design tokens only |
| **Icons:** Iconify `~icons/ic/outline-*` | DS-004 | No lucide-react/react-icons/heroicons |
| **Security headers:** `@emisgroup/acp-security-headers` in dependencies | WSEC-013 | pnpm add @emisgroup/acp-security-headers |
| **App discovery:** `applicationDiscovery` in package.json | AD-001 | See EMIS-X schema |
| **HTTP client:** `axios.create({ timeout: 30_000 })` — no fetch()/bare axios calls | HTTP-002a | Configured instance always |
| **No Node.js agents:** httpAgent/httpsAgent/keepAlive forbidden | HTTP-003a | Browser manages connections |
| **URL encoding:** `encodeURIComponent()` for all user-supplied URL values | WSEC-006a | No bare template literal interpolation |
| **i18n:** `t()` from react-i18next; translations in `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json` | WCS-007a | No hardcoded English strings in JSX |
| **British English:** translation JSON uses British spellings | WCS-007b | colour, centre, grey, behaviour, licence |
| **jest-axe:** `toHaveNoViolations()` in every component test file | A11Y-010 | Exempt: root.component, App, providers |
### Regulatory Framework
- **Clinical Safety:** Not safety-critical — DCB0129/0160 not applicable
- **Data Protection:** UK GDPR, Data Protection Act 2018
- **NHS Standards:** NHS DSPT (Data Security and Protection Toolkit)
- **Accessibility:** WCAG 2.1 Level AA (matching EMIS-X platform standard)
---
## Requirement Index
| ID | Name | Priority | Dimensions | Status |
|----|------|----------|------------|--------|
| [REQ-001](requirements/REQ-001.md) | Conversational Q&A Chat Widget | Must Have | IG, SEC, OBS, FE | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
| [REQ-002](requirements/REQ-002.md) | Escalation to Human Support | Must Have | IG, SEC, OBS, FE | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
| [REQ-003](requirements/REQ-003.md) | Full-Page Chat Mode | Must Have | SEC, OBS, FE | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
| [REQ-004](requirements/REQ-004.md) | Documentation Indexing via CI | Must Have | SEC, OBS | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
| [REQ-005](requirements/REQ-005.md) | Conversation Management | Must Have | IG, SEC, OBS, FE | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
| [REQ-006](requirements/REQ-006.md) | Bot Loading & Status States | Must Have | SEC, OBS, FE | ⏳ Pipeline 01 Complete |
**Total Requirements:** 6
**Must Have:** 6 | **Should Have:** 0 | **Could Have:** 0 | **Won''t Have:** 0
---
## Non-Functional Requirements
| Category | Requirement | Target |
|----------|-------------|--------|
| Performance | Bot response p95 latency | < 10,000ms |
| Performance | UI transition (widget ↔ full-page) | < 300ms |
| Performance | Escalation dispatch (webhook + email) | < 5s |
| Performance | Documentation indexing duration | < 5 minutes |
| Availability | Bot service uptime | 99.9% |
| Availability | Degraded mode | Bot outage → escalation form shown |
| Concurrency | Concurrent authenticated users | TBD — Pipeline 03 Architecture |
| Rate Limiting | Messages per session | 50 messages |
| Rate Limiting | Messages per user per day | 200 messages |
| Browser Support | Supported browsers/devices | Inherits EMIS-X platform matrix |
| Accessibility | WCAG level | 2.1 Level AA |
| Data Retention | Escalation records (email + chat history) | 1 year |
| Infrastructure | Cloud provider and region | AWS eu-west-2 |
| Cost | Implementation approach | Cost-optimised — Pipeline 03 to decide |
---
## Success Metrics
| Metric | Baseline | Target | Timeline | Measurement Method |
|--------|----------|--------|----------|--------------------|
| Sprint time spent answering interop questions | ~20% | < 5% | Post-launch (2 sprints) | Sprint time tracking |
| Bot answer rate (questions answered without escalation) | 0% | > 80% | 1 month post-launch | OTEL qabot.chat.query.complete |
| Escalation rate (conversations escalated to human) | 100% | < 20% | 1 month post-launch | OTEL qabot.escalation.triggered |
**North Star Metric:** Sprint time spent answering interop questions < 5%
---
## Constraints
### Regulatory Constraints
- UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018 — email addresses captured on escalation are personal data
- GDPR Article 6 lawful basis for escalation email processing: `[UNVERIFIED — IG-OWNER: TBD — RESOLUTION DATE: TBD — GO-LIVE BLOCKER]`
- Escalation data retention: 1 year maximum
- Data residency: AWS eu-west-2 (UK/EU compliant)
- WCAG 2.1 Level AA accessibility required
### Technical Constraints
- Must integrate with existing Astro/Starlight partner portal (React wrapper in place)
- Infrastructure: AWS only, eu-west-2 region
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions
- Email: AWS SES
- Notifications: Microsoft Teams webhook
- Frontend: EMIS-X platform standards (pnpm, @emisgroup/ui-*, design tokens)
- AI implementation approach: TBD — Pipeline 03 Architecture decision
### Business Constraints
- Cost-optimised implementation — lightweight/efficient AI approach preferred
- Partner developer experience must not be degraded during indexing or bot outage
### Timeline Constraints
- 2 sprints, timeboxed
---
## Key Assumptions & Risks
### High-Risk Assumptions
1. **AI implementation approach** — Risk: High — Validation: Pipeline 03 Architecture decision (LLM vs RAG vs embeddings vs fine-tuned model)
2. **Documentation corpus quality** — Risk: Medium — Assumption: Existing docs are accurate enough to index; bot reformulation will improve clarity not correctness
### Key Risks
1. **AI/ML implementation** — Likelihood: High — Impact: High — Mitigation: Pipeline 03 Architecture must decide approach before build starts; timeboxed to 2 sprints
2. **GDPR lawful basis unconfirmed** — Likelihood: Medium — Impact: High — Mitigation: IG owner must confirm before go-live; currently a GO-LIVE BLOCKER
3. **Teams webhook availability** — Likelihood: Low — Impact: Medium — Mitigation: User-visible error message on webhook failure; retry policy TBD in Pipeline 03
---
## Integration Points
| System | Purpose | Authentication | Data Flow | Failure Mode |
|--------|---------|---------------|-----------|--------------|
| Microsoft Teams (webhook) | Escalation notifications to internal team | Webhook URL (environment secret) | Outbound — email, chat history, page URL, timestamp | User sees "system unavailable, try later" message |
| AWS SES | Confirmation email to partner developer | AWS IAM (environment credentials) | Outbound — confirmation email | Silent failure — Teams webhook still fires |
| GitHub Actions | CI/CD pipeline for documentation indexing | Repository permissions + secrets | Triggered on portal update | Deployment blocked if indexing fails |
| EMIS-X Auth | Authentication for all chat access | EMIS-X OAuth2 | Inbound — session token validation | Redirect to EMIS-X login |
---
## Pipeline 01 → Pipeline 03 Handoff Notes
> Read this section before starting Pipeline 03. These are known blockers that affect Pipeline 03 scope.
### 🔴 Blockers — Do Not Skip
- **AI implementation approach undefined:** LLM, embeddings, fine-tuned model, or RAG — must be decided in Pipeline 03 before build starts. This is the highest risk item for the 2-sprint timebox.
- **GDPR Article 6 lawful basis unconfirmed:** Lawful basis for processing partner email addresses captured during escalation. IG-OWNER: TBD — RESOLUTION DATE: TBD — GO-LIVE BLOCKER.
### 🟡 Decisions to Clarify in Pipeline 03
- Teams channel webhook URL — needs to be configured before go-live
- Astro/Starlight + React wrapper component boundary — how does the chat bot integrate with the existing shell?
- Rate limiting enforcement point — client-side, API gateway, or bot service?
- Concurrent user capacity planning
- Index storage mechanism and artefact format (vector DB, JSON, etc.)
- AWS SES retry policy on failure
- Teams webhook retry policy on failure
### 🟢 Deferred Items
- Full WCAG 2.1 AA audit — Pipeline 05 PxD
- Detailed UI/UX specifications — Pipeline 05 PxD
- API contract definitions (OpenAPI) — Pipeline 04 Design
- Full hazard/mitigation mapping — N/A (not safety-critical)
---
**Document Status:** ✅ Pipeline 01 Requirements Complete
**Pipeline Status:** Pipeline 01 ✅ → Pipeline 03 ⏳ → Pipeline 04 ⏳ → Pipeline 05 ⏳ → Pipeline 06 ⏳ → Pipeline 07 ⏳ → Pipeline 08 ⏳ → Coding Agent
**Next Phase:** Pipeline 03 Architecture (adds technical architecture to each requirement)
**Pipeline:** Pipeline 01 → Pipeline 03 → Pipeline 04 → Pipeline 05 → Pipeline 06 → Pipeline 07 → Pipeline 08 → Coding Agent
