INSERT INTO artefact (artefact_id, project_id, version, file_path, content_type, content, size_bytes, created_by, created_at) VALUES ('7e0e27e4-f4ff-4435-942a-11df96592c86', '03735ad1-8759-414e-a93f-ce8cc7bfc1fc', 1, 'requirements/REQ-005.md', 'text/markdown', '# REQ-005: Conversation Management
**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Low
**Risk:** Low
**Depends On:** REQ-001, REQ-003
---
## User Story
As an external partner developer,
I need my conversation history to persist across pages and views within my session, and to be clearable on demand or on browser close,
So that I can continue a conversation naturally without losing context, and start fresh when I choose.
**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Conversation history persists across page navigation within the same browser session
- [ ] Conversation history persists between widget and full-page views within the same session
- [ ] An explicit "Clear conversation" button is available in both the widget and full-page view
- [ ] Clicking "Clear conversation" immediately resets the conversation to a clean state (confirmation prompt shown before clearing)
- [ ] Closing the browser clears the conversation — no history persists on next visit
---
## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety
### Applicable Guardrails
- N/A — system is not safety-critical
### Hazards Addressed
- None identified
### Mitigations
- None required
---
## Dimension 2: Information Governance
### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — conversation data held in sessionStorage only, not persisted server-side
### GDPR Articles
- **Article 6 Lawful Basis:** N/A — no server-side personal data storage for conversation content
- **Article 9 Special Category:** N/A
### Data Handling Requirements
- **Data Categories:** Conversation messages (non-personal in most cases)
- **Data Subjects:** External partner developers
- **Retention Period:** Session only — cleared on browser close
- **Data Minimisation:** No conversation data written to server; sessionStorage scoped to tab/window
---
## Dimension 3: Security
### Applicable Guardrails
- **SEC-001:** TLS encryption in transit for all HTTP
- **WSEC-006a:** encodeURIComponent() for any user-supplied URL values
### Security Requirements
- **Authentication:** EMIS-X authentication required (inherited from REQ-001, REQ-003)
- **Authorisation:** Authenticated EMIS-X users only
- **Encryption in Transit:** TLS 1.2+ for all HTTP
- **Encryption at Rest:** N/A — conversation data not persisted server-side; sessionStorage used client-side only
- **Storage:** sessionStorage (not localStorage) — scoped to tab/window, cleared on browser close
---
## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance
### Product KPIs
- **KPI 1:** Clear conversation event rate — baseline: unknown, target: measurable within sprint 1
- **KPI 2:** Average session duration — baseline: unknown, target: measurable within sprint 1
- **KPI 3:** Average conversation length (message count) — baseline: unknown, target: measurable within sprint 1
### Observable Events (OTEL Instrumentation)
- **Span 1:** `qabot.conversation.clear.start`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, message_count_before_clear, trigger (button/browser_close)
- **Span 2:** `qabot.conversation.clear.complete`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, duration_ms, status
### Performance SLOs
- **Latency p95:** < 300ms for clear action
- **Availability:** 99.9%
- **Error Rate:** < 0.1%
### Alerting Conditions
- **Warning:** Clear action fails to reset state → Slack/Teams notification
---
## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification
**PURPOSE:** Define DETERMINISTIC pass/fail criteria for coding agents to verify implementation.
---
### CHECK 1: Session Persistence Across Navigation
**Trigger:** User navigates between pages within the same browser session
**Test Scenario 1: Conversation persists across page navigation**
- **Setup:** Authenticated EMIS-X user sends 3 messages in the widget on page A
- **Action:** User navigates to page B
- **Expected:** Widget shows same 3 messages
- **Validation:** Message count and content identical before and after navigation
**Test Scenario 2: Conversation persists between widget and full-page view**
- **Setup:** Authenticated EMIS-X user sends 2 messages in widget
- **Action:** User expands to full-page view
- **Expected:** Full-page view shows same 2 messages
- **Pass Criteria:** Conversation state shared across views within session
**Applicable Guardrail:** IG-001 (Data Minimisation — sessionStorage only)
**Pass Criteria:** Conversation history intact across navigation and view transitions
---
### CHECK 2: Clear Conversation Button
**Trigger:** User clicks "Clear conversation" button
**Test Scenario 1: Confirmation prompt shown before clearing**
- **Input:** User clicks "Clear conversation"
- **Expected:** Confirmation prompt appears before any data is cleared
- **Validation:** Conversation history still visible at prompt stage
**Test Scenario 2: Conversation cleared on confirmation**
- **Input:** User confirms clear action
- **Expected Response:** Conversation resets to empty state
- **Validation:** Message count = 0, sessionStorage key cleared
- **Timing:** Clear action completes < 300ms
**Test Scenario 3: Cancel does not clear**
- **Input:** User clicks "Clear conversation" then cancels
- **Expected:** Conversation history unchanged
- **Pass Criteria:** Cancel preserves all messages
**Applicable Guardrail:** DS-001 (@emisgroup/ui-* components for button and confirmation dialog)
**Pass Criteria:** Clear requires confirmation, executes within 300ms, cancellable
---
### CHECK 3: Browser Close Clears Conversation
**Trigger:** User closes browser tab/window
**Test Scenario 1: No persistence after browser close**
- **Setup:** User has active conversation with 5 messages
- **Action:** Close browser, reopen portal, navigate to same page
- **Expected:** Widget shows empty conversation (no previous messages)
- **Validation:** sessionStorage key does not exist on new session
- **Anti-pattern:** localStorage used instead of sessionStorage (localStorage persists across browser close)
**Applicable Guardrail:** IG-001 (Data Minimisation)
**Pass Criteria:** sessionStorage used (not localStorage); conversation cleared on browser close
---
### CHECK 4: DS-001 — @emisgroup Components Only
**Trigger:** Any rendered UI element for clear button or confirmation dialog
**Test Scenario:** No native HTML interactive elements
- **Validation 1:** No `<button>` elements — use `@emisgroup/ui-Button`
- **Validation 2:** No `<dialog>` elements — use `@emisgroup/ui-Dialog` or equivalent
- **Anti-pattern:** `<button onClick={clearConversation}>Clear</button>`
**Applicable Guardrail:** DS-001
**Pass Criteria:** All interactive elements use @emisgroup/ui-* components
---
### CHECK 5: WCS-007a — i18n for All UI Text
**Trigger:** Any user-facing string in conversation management UI
**Test Scenario:** All strings use t() from react-i18next
- **Validation 1:** "Clear conversation" button label uses `t(''conversation.clear.button'')`
- **Validation 2:** Confirmation prompt text uses `t(''conversation.clear.confirm'')`
- **Validation 3:** Translation keys exist in `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json`
- **Validation 4:** British English spellings used in translation JSON
**Applicable Guardrail:** WCS-007a, WCS-007b
**Pass Criteria:** No hardcoded English strings in JSX; all keys in en-GB translation file
---
### CHECK 6: A11Y-010 — jest-axe Accessibility
**Trigger:** Component test file for conversation management UI
**Test Scenario:** jest-axe passes with no violations
- **Validation 1:** `import { axe, toHaveNoViolations } from ''jest-axe''` present in test file
- **Validation 2:** `expect(results).toHaveNoViolations()` called in at least one test
- **Validation 3:** Clear button has accessible label (`aria-label` or `htmlFor`)
- **Validation 4:** Confirmation dialog has accessible role (`role="dialog"`, `aria-labelledby`)
**Applicable Guardrail:** A11Y-010, A11Y-004a
**Pass Criteria:** jest-axe passes with zero violations; all interactive elements accessible
---
## Traceability
| Requirement | Hazard | Mitigation | Guardrail | Evaluation Check |
|-------------|--------|------------|-----------|------------------|
| REQ-005 | — | sessionStorage only | IG-001 | CHECK 3 |
| REQ-005 | — | Confirmation before clear | DS-001 | CHECK 2 |
| REQ-005 | — | Session persistence | IG-001 | CHECK 1 |
| REQ-005 | — | @emisgroup components | DS-001 | CHECK 4 |
| REQ-005 | — | i18n / British English | WCS-007a, WCS-007b | CHECK 5 |
| REQ-005 | — | Accessibility | A11Y-010 | CHECK 6 |
---
## Change Log
| Version | Date | Agent | Changes |
|---------|------|-------|---------|
| 1.0 | 2026-05-31 | Pipeline 01 Requirements | Initial creation |
**Pipeline Status:**
- ✅ Pipeline 01 Complete (Requirements with eval specs)
- ⏳ Pipeline 03 Pending (Architecture)
- ⏳ Pipeline 04 Pending (Design — API contracts, DB schemas)
- ⏳ Pipeline 05 Pending (PxD — UI/UX specifications)
- ⏳ Pipeline 06 Pending (Clinical Safety — N/A for this system)
- ⏳ Pipeline 07 Pending (Normalisation — Transform to JSON)
- ⏳ Pipeline 08 Pending (Planning — Dependency-ordered tasks)
', 9028, 'ern:emis:user:user:7ae7b859-c480-4644-b3be-d77d628f6e7e', '2026-05-31 19:37:16.000289+00');
INSERT INTO artefact (artefact_id, project_id, version, file_path, content_type, content, size_bytes, created_by, created_at) VALUES ('55a5c2d3-572b-4563-92d0-1e4f94e79b90', '03735ad1-8759-414e-a93f-ce8cc7bfc1fc', 1, 'requirements/REQ-006.md', 'text/markdown', '# REQ-006: Bot Loading & Status States
**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Low
**Risk:** Low
**Depends On:** REQ-001
---
## User Story
As an external partner developer,
I need to see what the bot is doing while it processes my question,
So that I know the system is working and am not left staring at a blank screen for up to 10 seconds.
**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] While the bot is processing a response, a loading spinner is displayed in the chat interface
- [ ] When the bot is executing tool calls (e.g. searching documentation, retrieving examples), a contextual status message is shown to the user (e.g. "Searching documentation…", "Retrieving examples…")
- [ ] Status messages update in real-time as the bot progresses through tool calls
- [ ] Spinner and status messages disappear when the response is ready
- [ ] If the bot times out (>10s), a polite error message is shown: "Sorry, that''s taking longer than expected. Please try again or escalate to our team."
---
## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety
### Applicable Guardrails
- N/A — system is not safety-critical (confirmed Phase 2)
### Hazards Addressed
- None identified
### Mitigations
- None required
---
## Dimension 2: Information Governance
### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-001:** Data Minimisation — status messages must not expose internal system details
### GDPR Articles
- **Article 6 Lawful Basis:** N/A — no personal data captured in loading states
- **Article 9 Special Category:** N/A
### Data Handling Requirements
- **Data Categories:** None
- **Data Subjects:** None
- **Retention Period:** N/A
- **Data Minimisation:** Status messages must not expose internal tool call details, API endpoints, or system internals
---
## Dimension 3: Security
### Applicable Guardrails
- **SEC-001:** TLS 1.2+ for all HTTP communication
- **WSEC-006a:** encodeURIComponent() for any user-supplied URL values
### Security Requirements
- **Authentication:** EMIS-X authentication required (inherited from REQ-001)
- **Authorisation:** Authenticated EMIS-X users only
- **Encryption in Transit:** TLS 1.2+
- **Encryption at Rest:** N/A — no data persisted
- **Information Leakage:** Status messages MUST NOT expose internal system details, tool names, API endpoints, or error stack traces
---
## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance
### Product KPIs
- **KPI 1:** Spinner appearance latency — Target: < 300ms after question submission
- **KPI 2:** Timeout rate — Target: < 5% of requests
- **KPI 3:** Tool call duration per type — Baseline: TBD, Target: < 8s per tool call
### Observable Events (OTEL Instrumentation)
- **Span 1:** `qabot.loading.spinner.start`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, question_length, timestamp
- **Span 2:** `qabot.loading.toolcall.start`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, tool_name (sanitised), timestamp
- **Span 3:** `qabot.loading.toolcall.complete`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, tool_name (sanitised), duration_ms, status
- **Span 4:** `qabot.loading.timeout`
  - **Attributes:** session_id, elapsed_ms, timestamp
### Performance SLOs
- **Spinner appearance:** < 300ms after question submission
- **Availability:** 99.9%
- **Timeout rate:** < 5%
### Alerting Conditions
- **Critical:** Timeout rate > 10% over 5 minutes → Slack/Teams alert
- **Warning:** p95 spinner appearance > 500ms → Warning alert
---
## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification
**PURPOSE:** Define DETERMINISTIC pass/fail criteria for coding agents to verify implementation.
---
### CHECK 1: Spinner Appearance Timing
**Trigger:** User submits a question to the bot
**Test Scenario 1: Spinner appears promptly**
- **Setup:** Authenticated EMIS-X user with open chat session
- **Input:** User submits question "Which auth flow should I use for a backend API?"
- **Expected:** Loading spinner visible within 300ms of submission
- **Validation:** Measure time from submit event to spinner render — must be < 300ms
**Test Scenario 2: Spinner disappears on response**
- **Input:** Bot completes processing and returns response
- **Expected:** Spinner removed from DOM, response text displayed
- **Validation:** Spinner element not present after response renders
**Guardrail:** WCS-007a (i18n for status text)
**Pass Criteria:** Spinner appears < 300ms, disappears on response
---
### CHECK 2: Tool Call Status Messages
**Trigger:** Bot executes a tool call during processing
**Test Scenario 1: Status message shown during tool call**
- **Setup:** Bot processing a question that requires a documentation search
- **Expected:** Status message visible: "Searching documentation…"
- **Validation:** Status message element present in DOM during tool call execution
**Test Scenario 2: Status message updates across multiple tool calls**
- **Setup:** Bot executes two tool calls sequentially
- **Expected:** Status message updates to reflect each tool call in sequence
- **Validation:** Message text changes between tool calls
**Test Scenario 3: Status message does not expose internals**
- **Expected:** Status message contains only user-friendly text — no API endpoint names, internal function names, or stack traces
- **Validation:** Message text matches approved strings from translation.json only
**Guardrail:** IG-001 (no internal detail leakage), WCS-007a (i18n)
**Pass Criteria:** Status messages shown, updated, and contain only approved user-friendly text
---
### CHECK 3: Timeout Handling
**Trigger:** Bot processing exceeds 10 seconds
**Test Scenario 1: Timeout error message shown**
- **Setup:** Mock bot response delayed > 10s
- **Expected Response:** Polite error message displayed: "Sorry, that''s taking longer than expected. Please try again or escalate to our team."
- **Validation:** Error message visible, spinner removed, escalation prompt accessible
**Test Scenario 2: Timeout does not crash session**
- **Expected:** Conversation remains intact after timeout; user can submit another question
- **Validation:** Chat input re-enabled after timeout message shown
**Guardrail:** WCS-007a (i18n for error text)
**Pass Criteria:** Timeout surfaces polite error, session remains usable
---
### CHECK 4: A11Y-007a — Live Region for Status Messages
**Trigger:** Any loading or status state rendered
**Test Scenario: Screen reader announcement**
- **Validation 1:** Status message container has `aria-live="polite"` or `role="status"`
- **Validation 2:** Spinner has accessible label (aria-label or aria-labelledby)
- **Validation 3:** Timeout error has `role="alert"` for immediate announcement
**Guardrail:** A11Y-007a
**Pass Criteria:** All dynamic states announced to screen readers
---
### CHECK 5: A11Y-010 — jest-axe Accessibility
**Trigger:** Component render in test suite
**Test Scenario: No accessibility violations**
- **Validation:** `jest-axe` `toHaveNoViolations()` passes for loading spinner component, status message component, and timeout error component
**Guardrail:** A11Y-010
**Pass Criteria:** Zero axe violations in all loading state components
---
### CHECK 6: DS-001 — @emisgroup/ui-* Components
**Trigger:** Component implementation review
**Validation:** No native HTML `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, `<dialog>` used in loading state components — all interactive elements use `@emisgroup/ui-*`
**Guardrail:** DS-001
**Pass Criteria:** Only @emisgroup/ui-* components used
---
### CHECK 7: WCS-007a / WCS-007b — i18n and British English
**Trigger:** Any user-facing string in loading state components
**Validation 1:** All status messages use `t()` from react-i18next — no hardcoded strings in JSX
**Validation 2:** Translation keys present in `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json`
**Validation 3:** British English spellings used (e.g. "Searching" not misspelled; check for colour/centre/grey patterns where applicable)
**Guardrail:** WCS-007a, WCS-007b
**Pass Criteria:** All strings externalised to translation.json with British English spellings
---
## Traceability
| Requirement | Hazard | Mitigation | Guardrail | Evaluation Check |
|-------------|--------|------------|-----------|------------------|
| REQ-006 | — | Spinner < 300ms | WCS-007a | CHECK 1 |
| REQ-006 | — | Tool call status messages | IG-001 | CHECK 2 |
| REQ-006 | — | Timeout error handling | WCS-007a | CHECK 3 |
| REQ-006 | — | Live regions for a11y | A11Y-007a | CHECK 4 |
| REQ-006 | — | jest-axe no violations | A11Y-010 | CHECK 5 |
| REQ-006 | — | @emisgroup components | DS-001 | CHECK 6 |
| REQ-006 | — | i18n + British English | WCS-007a, WCS-007b | CHECK 7 |
---
## Change Log
| Version | Date | Agent | Changes |
|---------|------|-------|---------|
| 1.0 | 2026-05-31 | Pipeline 01 Requirements | Initial creation |
**Pipeline Status:**
- ✅ Pipeline 01 Complete (Requirements with eval specs)
- ⏳ Pipeline 03 Pending (Architecture)
- ⏳ Pipeline 04 Pending (Design — API contracts, DB schemas)
- ⏳ Pipeline 05 Pending (PxD — UI/UX specifications)
- ⏳ Pipeline 06 Pending (Clinical Safety — Full hazard/mitigation mapping)
- ⏳ Pipeline 07 Pending (Normalisation — Transform to JSON)
- ⏳ Pipeline 08 Pending (Planning — Dependency-ordered task plan)
